Arenula MCP is licensed per component, not as a single work. There is no one
license covering this repository, which is why this file points at the three
that actually apply rather than declaring a fourth.

    editor/     GPL-3.0-only   see editor/LICENSE
    api/        MIT            see api/LICENSE
    docs/       MIT            see docs/LICENSE
    schemagen/  MIT            see schemagen/LICENSE

The split is deliberate and not merely historical. The editor plugin is a
derivative of the Ozmium MCP Server for s&box (https://github.com/ozmium7/
ozmium-mcp-server-for-sbox), which is GPL-3.0, so the editor component
inherits GPL-3.0 and cannot be relicensed. The API and docs servers derive
from sbox-api-mcp and sbox-docs-mcp by sofianebel, both MIT, and stay MIT.

The schemagen/ sidecar is original work with no upstream to inherit from, so
it is MIT: it is a standalone .NET reflector, useful independently of the
editor plugin that invokes it.

If you vendor part of this repository, take the license of the directory you
copied from. Copying the editor into an MIT project does not make it MIT.

Contributions are licensed under the license of the component being modified;
see CONTRIBUTING.md.

